

-- ===========================================================================
-- Warlock: Infernal Bargain becomes a channel
-- ===========================================================================
--
-- Supersedes the instant version from woa_2026_08_01_06.sql (and its tooltip
-- fixes in woa_2026_08_01_08.sql).  The talent was an instant that dumped up
-- to 16 Soul Shards at once; it is now an Evocation-style channel:
--
--   6 second self-channel, one tick every 1.5 sec  -> exactly 4 ticks
--   1 Soul Shard per tick, 1 buff stack per shard, stacks applied live
--   15/20/25% damage reduction FOR THE DURATION OF THE CHANNEL ONLY
--   10 second stacking buff afterwards
--
-- RANK SPELLS 63349 / 63350 / 63351
--   AttributesEx 64 = SPELL_ATTR1_IS_SELF_CHANNELED (SharedDefines.h:413),
--   the same bit Evocation (12051) uses; SpellInfo::IsChanneled() keys off it.
--   DurationIndex 27 = 6000ms, sourced from Hammer of Justice (853).
--   (Cross-checked: 28 = 5000 Drain Life, 31 = 8000 Evocation + Rain of Fire,
--    1 = 10000, 21 = permanent.)
--
--   Effect1 = SPELL_AURA_PERIODIC_DUMMY, EffectAmplitude1 1500.
--     AuraEffect::GetTotalTicks() is MaxDuration / amplitude = 6000/1500 = 4
--     (SpellAuraEffects.cpp:7064) and the per-tick guard is
--     (m_tickNumber + 1) > totalTicks (SpellAuraEffects.cpp:935), so the tick
--     landing exactly at 6000ms still fires.  The first tick is at 1500, not
--     0, because CalculatePeriodic does m_periodicTimer += m_amplitude.
--     Handled by spell_warl_infernal_bargain_aura (src/WarlockInfernalBargain.cpp).
--
--   Effect2 = SPELL_AURA_MOD_DAMAGE_PERCENT_TAKEN, MiscValue 127 (all schools).
--     This is the whole trick for "protected only while channeling": the aura
--     lives on the CHANNEL, so its lifetime is the channel's lifetime and it
--     falls off by itself.  Zero C++ involved.  Stored negative because
--     MOD_DAMAGE_PERCENT_TAKEN reduces damage with a negative amount;
--     BasePoints -16/-21/-26 with DieSides 1 -> CalcValue -15/-20/-25.
--
--   EffectTriggerSpell1 carries the rank's buff id.  SPELL_AURA_PERIODIC_DUMMY
--   never auto-triggers it (the tick dispatcher only routes TriggerSpell for
--   PERIODIC_TRIGGER_SPELL*), so it is a free, data-driven rank -> buff map
--   and the C++ needs no rank switch.
--
--   ChannelInterruptFlags 3084 (0xC0C = CAST|MOVE|TALK|USE) is Evocation's
--   31756 minus three bits: 0x4000 (pushback-on-damage -- Alonecraft removes
--   casting pushback, see src/Pushback.cpp) and 0x1000/0x2000 (MELEE_ATTACK /
--   SPELL_ATTACK, which fire when the CASTER attacks -- a warlock with
--   auto-attack on would shatter their own 2 minute cooldown instantly).
--
--   Effect3 is fully zeroed.  It used to be a pure data carrier holding the
--   damage reduction (BasePoints 14/19/24); leaving it would strand a stale
--   $s3 in the tooltip.  RecoveryTime stays 120000 (2 min).
--
-- BUFF SPELLS 200401 (R1) / 200404 (R2) / 200405 (R3)
--   One buff per rank instead of one shared buff with script-supplied custom
--   basepoints.  AuraEffect::CalculateAmount ends with an unconditional
--   "amount *= GetBase()->GetStackAmount()" (SpellAuraEffects.cpp:580), so
--   fixed per-stack basepoints + StackAmount 4 means the engine does all the
--   scaling and the script just casts the right id.
--
--     Effect1 = MOD_DAMAGE_PERCENT_DONE (MiscValue 127)  2 / 3 / 4 % per stack
--     Effect2 = MOD_SPELL_CRIT_CHANCE                    1 / 1 / 2 % per stack
--
--   BasePoints are N-1 with DieSides 1 per the project convention.
--   DurationIndex 1 = 10000ms.  Aura::ModStackAmount refreshes the duration on
--   every increment (SpellAuras.cpp:981-987), so a full channel already ends
--   with the full 10s; the script tops it up on the early-exit paths.
--
--   The old Effect3 of 200401 was MOD_DAMAGE_PERCENT_TAKEN -- it MUST be gone,
--   or the reduction would persist after the channel and defeat the redesign.
--   Every EffectSpellClassMask is zeroed (the --base cloning pitfall).
-- ===========================================================================


